  "id": "Compound::DB01380 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Cortisone Acetate is linked to Cyp3a4 through a series of biological pathways involving corticosteroid hormone receptor agonists. The evidence suggests that Cortisone Acetate, as a member of the corticosteroid hormone receptor agonists family, binds to the corticosteroid hormone receptor, which in turn activates downstream signaling that ultimately leads to the expression of Cyp3a4. This mechanism is consistent across multiple paths, as all three members of the corticosteroid hormone receptor agonists family—Fluorometholone, Budesonide, and Triamcinolone—share a common pathway to Cyp3a4. The lowest common ancestors of these entities, both in the corticosteroid hormone receptor agonists and the therapeutic glucocorticoid category, reinforce the hierarchical relationship between the drug and the enzyme. The integrated evidence highlights a recurring mechanism of receptor activation leading to enzyme induction, suggesting that Cortisone Acetate may exert its effect through a similar pathway, thereby supporting a direct relationship between the drug and Cyp3a4.",
